workedExamples.question_text:
A circle has an area of $80\text{ cm}^{2}$. Find its radius to 2 decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.5);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw (0,0)--(40:1.5) node[midway,below right] {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A semicircle has an area of $32\text{ m}^{2}$. Find its radius to 3 decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (-1.8,0)--(1.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.8];
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (0.9,0) {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A quadrant has an area of $18\text{ mm}^{2}$. Find its radius to 2 decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2]--cycle;
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circle has an area of $50\text{ mm}^{2}$. Find its diameter to 2 decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.5);
\draw (-1.5,0)--(1.5,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above] at (0,0.15) {$d$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A semicircle has an area of $24\text{ cm}^{2}$. Find its diameter to 2 decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (-1.8,0)--(1.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.8];
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (0,-0.15) {$d$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A quadrant has an area of $16\pi\text{ cm}^{2}$. Find its exact radius.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2]--cycle;
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A sector has an area of $27\pi\text{ cm}^{2}$ and an angle at the centre of $120^{\circ}$. Find its exact radius and diameter.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(2.2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=120,radius=2.2]--cycle;
\draw (0.45,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=120,radius=0.45];
\node at (60:0.95) {$120^{\circ}$};
\node[below] at (1.1,0) {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A sector has an area of $48\pi\text{ cm}^{2}$ and a radius of $8\text{ cm}$. Find its interior angle $\theta$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=270,radius=2]--cycle;
\draw (0.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=270,radius=0.5];
\node at (135:0.9) {$\theta$};
\node[above] at (1,0) {$8\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two circles have the same centre. The larger circle has diameter $24\text{ cm}$. The region between the circles has area $80\pi\text{ cm}^{2}$. Find the exact diameter of the smaller circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (0,0) circle (1.8);
\fill[white] (0,0) circle (1.2);
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.8);
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.2);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw (0,0)--(1.2,0) node[midway,above] {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

